      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "@ozbillwang yep.\n\nthe only change I needed:\n```\n#FROM python:3.9-alpine\nFROM python:3.12-alpine\n```\nThis did a switch to Python 3.12.7\n\nHere is the throughput on my desktop PC (as said, it is  the same as for Python 3.9 though) :\n\n```\n...\nsampler seed: 1846266218\nsampler params:\n\trepeat_last_n = 64, repeat_penalty = 1.000, frequency_penalty = 0.000, presence_penalty = 0.000\n\ttop_k = 40, tfs_z = 1.000, top_p = 0.950, min_p = 0.050, typical_p = 1.000, temp = 0.800\n\tmirostat = 0, mirostat_lr = 0.100, mirostat_ent = 5.000\nsampler chain: logits -> logit-bias -> penalties -> top-k -> tail-free -> typical -> top-p -> min-p -> temp-ext -> softmax -> dist\ngenerate: n_ctx = 2048, n_batch = 1, n_predict = 128, n_keep = 1\n\nThe meaning to life and the universe is not a matter of chance. It is a matter of the will of God. It was the will of God that there should be a universe, and it is the will of God that this universe should not be without life. God is the source of all life, and therefore He is the source of all that is good, and therefore good is not a matter of chance. God is the source of all the good, and therefore God is the source of all the beautiful, the true, the lovely, the just, the good, and the true. It is the will of God that all men should be saved. It is the will\n\nllama_perf_sampler_print:    sampling time =       7.25 ms /   137 runs   (    0.05 ms per token, 18886.13 tokens per second)\nllama_perf_context_print:        load time =     609.15 ms\nllama_perf_context_print: prompt eval time =     709.52 ms /     9 tokens (   78.84 ms per token,    12.68 tokens per second)\nllama_perf_context_print:        eval time =    9956.22 ms /   127 runs   (   78.40 ms per token,    12.76 tokens per second)\n```",
